      "hints": [
        "Let $u = x^{1/2}$ to get quadratic $4u^2 - 11u + 6 = 0$.",
        "Factorise: $(4u - 3)(u - 2) = 0 \\implies u = \\frac{3}{4}, 2$.",
        "Square roots: $x = \\frac{9}{16}, 4$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $u = x^{1/2}$ (so $u^2 = x$) to transform the equation into a quadratic:\n$$4u^2 - 11u + 6 = 0$$",
        "Factorise and solve for $u$:\n$$(4u - 3)(u - 2) = 0 \\implies u = \\frac{3}{4} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad u = 2$$",
        "Square both values of $u$ to find $x$:\n$$x^{1/2} = \\frac{3}{4} \\implies x = \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{9}{16}$$\n$$x^{1/2} = 2 \\implies x = 2^2 = 4$$\n$$\\text{Solutions: } x = \\frac{9}{16}, \\quad 4$$"
      ],
